Its a low cost, low powered system on a chip , micro controller(A microcontroller is a small computer built onto a single chip to control electronic devices.) created by Espressif system that features integrated bluetooth and wifi.It can
  1)Read input from sensors and microphones.
  2)Process instructions using its CPU cores.
  3)Connect to Wi-Fi and Bluetooth.
  4)Control LEDs, motors, and other devices.
>>Processor:- Dual core CPU or single core ,32 bit microprocessor running upto 240 Mhz(One instruction may take one clock cycle or multiple cycles, depending on the processor and instruction). 
>>Connectivty :- Built in 2.4 GHz Wifi and  BLuetooth BLE/Classic.
>>Power management:- very low power consumption.
>>Peripherals: 
      -Set of GPIO(General-Purpose Input/Output) pins,Used to read inputs or control outputs.Ex:- Read a button press or turn an LED on.Read Digital Sensors:-Interfacing with motion detectors,temp sensor , humidity sensor to gather real data : Output: Triggering leds,sounding buzzers.
      -ADC(analog to Digital Converters) ,Real-Life Example: Reading a Potentiometer or Temperature Sensor (like LM35).
      -DAC ( Digital to Analog Converters) ,Real-Life Example: Playing Music through an Audio Speaker or Generating Audio Tones.
      -I2C(Inter-Integrated Circuit)- used to connect devices like OLED screens or digital environmental sensors (ex- temperature, pressure, and humidity sensor) using only those two wires (SDA for data and SCL for the clock signal).
      -UART(Universal Asynchronous Receiver-Transmitter)-Transfers serial data between devices using TX (transmit) and RX (receive) lines.
      -SPI(Serial Peripheral Interface)-that demand fast data transfers—like colorful TFT display screens, SD cards, or external flash memory.
      -PWM (Pulse Width Modulation) -Controlling LED brightness or motor speed.
      -Timers and counters
      -I²S (Inter-IC Sound) - Transfers digital audio between compatible devices.
      -Touch sensing - Detects changes in capacitance when a finger approaches or touches a supported touch pad.
      -Watchdog timer - Helps recover a system if software gets stuck and fails to respond within the required time.

>>Programming:- Arduino IDE, micropython, circuitpython , native ESP- IDE.
>>Uses:- IOT.
>>Clock Speed:- Running upto 240 MHz.
>>SRAM Memory - static random access memory - 520 KB of internal RAM.
>>Flash Memory : 4 to 16 MB.
